  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{3}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, let $u=x+4.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,\u27f9\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe can now rewrite the integral in terms of $u,$ solve it, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|u|+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|x+4|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
